S={
"aggarwal25_interspeech":("meaning-and-interaction","dialogue-and-social-speech","conversational-grounding","An interview coach must judge whether a spoken answer addresses the interpersonal question, not merely whether its words are grammatical.","Interview answers depend on context, social intent, turn history, and domain knowledge that surface lexical matching misses.","Ask a general language model to answer from the transcript alone and treat fluent text as understanding.","Evaluate large language models on spoken-interaction reasoning with explicit contextual knowledge and prompt structure.","Supply interview context and domain knowledge, compare prompting strategies and model scales, and score both answer quality and reasoning behavior.","Prompt conditions act as information controls: context and domain knowledge reduce ambiguity, while ablations reveal which information supports the decision.","VetTrain interview data are used with quantitative and qualitative evaluation, model-size comparisons, and prompt ablations involving domain knowledge and interaction context.","The paper reports that contextual and domain-knowledge prompting improves selected spoken-interaction reasoning settings, especially for larger models.","Interview distribution, transcript quality, subjective scoring, prompt sensitivity, and model-family coverage limit claims about general conversational understanding."),
"kang25b_interspeech":("voice-generation-and-control","voice-conversion-and-identity","cross-domain-voice-conversion","A voice converter should carry identity and expressive qualities across human, animal, or designed sound domains without collapsing the target sound.","Source and target domains differ in pitch structure, timbre, articulation, and available parallel data.","Copy a human speaker embedding into the target domain or train paired conversion on a narrow set of source and target voices.","Learn high-fidelity cross-domain conversion that preserves controllable identity cues while generating a plausible target-domain signal.","Separate content-like and identity-like evidence, condition generation on the desired target sound, and evaluate both acoustic fidelity and perceptual identity.","The conversion mapping must preserve information useful for the target domain while discarding source-domain artifacts; perceptual judgments test whether this tradeoff is believable.","The paper evaluates human-to-animal and designed-sound conversion with objective audio comparisons and listener judgments against conversion baselines.","The authors report improved fidelity and plausibility for cross-domain conversion, while the unusual targets expose failures hidden by ordinary human voice-conversion benchmarks.","Sparse target data, subjective evaluation, target-domain definitions, and unclear physical correspondence limit claims of general voice conversion."),
"mohsin25_interspeech":("evaluation-deployment-and-consequence","fairness-and-social-risk","generative-bias-audit","A text-to-audio generator should not turn neutral prompts into systematically gendered sound or reproduce stereotypes as if they were acoustic facts.","Training captions and web audio encode social stereotypes, and a plausible sample can conceal unequal behavior across prompt groups.","Report aggregate generation quality and assume that a named model is neutral unless an obvious failure is heard.","Define a measurable gender-bias audit for text-to-audio outputs and compare model behavior across controlled prompts.","Generate matched prompt sets, classify or rate gendered attributes, and aggregate the results into a bias score that makes asymmetry visible.","The audit compares conditional output distributions rather than a single sample; the metric converts a social-risk question into a reproducible disparity measurement.","Multiple text-to-audio systems and controlled prompt sets are evaluated with the proposed gender-bias metric and qualitative inspection.","The paper reports frequent gender bias that reflects training-data stereotypes and argues for explicit bias evaluation in text-to-audio systems.","Gender labels, annotator assumptions, prompt coverage, model versions, and the proposed metric's validity limit causal or cultural conclusions."),
"tian25_interspeech":("meaning-and-interaction","grounding-and-action","audio-token-semantics","An audio captioner must preserve sound events in a compact representation while giving a language decoder enough evidence to describe them.","Audio contains simultaneous events and fine timing, but a caption model must compress it before generating variable-length language.","Use one continuous embedding or a generic tokenizer and assume reconstruction preserves whatever captioning needs.","Compare discrete audio representations for caption generation and test whether tokenization retains semantic evidence.","Encode audio into learned discrete tokens, condition a text decoder on those tokens, and compare tokenizers and decoder choices on caption metrics.","Quantization creates a finite vocabulary of acoustic units; the central question is whether the units preserve event identity rather than merely waveform detail.","Experiments on Clotho compare discrete tokenization methods and captioning systems with standard automatic caption metrics and representation ablations.","The paper reports that selected audio tokenizers improve automated captioning quality, showing that representation design affects semantic generation.","Reference-caption incompleteness, metric proxy limits, dataset scope, and no broad human grounding study limit conclusions about listener usefulness."),
"xu25_interspeech":("meaning-and-interaction","grounding-and-action","diverse-caption-generation","An audio captioner should describe the same sound accurately in several natural ways instead of producing one brittle sentence or repeating training phrasing.","Sound events are ambiguous and captions are one-to-many: several descriptions can be correct while lexical metrics prefer one wording.","Use a deterministic autoregressive decoder and optimize likelihood toward a single reference style.","Use diffusion-based caption generation to model multiple plausible descriptions while retaining event fidelity.","Condition iterative denoising on audio representations, sample candidate text representations, and decode captions whose diversity can be measured alongside quality.","Diffusion represents a distribution over possible captions; sampling exposes the tradeoff between semantic accuracy, diversity, and computation.","DAC is evaluated on audio-captioning benchmarks with caption-quality and diversity metrics, efficiency comparisons, and ablations of the diffusion design.","The paper reports stronger caption quality and diversity than comparison systems, with the stochastic decoder offering broader descriptions.","Automatic diversity can reward irrelevant variation, sampling cost matters, references are incomplete, and benchmark audio limits transfer."),
"xu25b_interspeech":("listening-and-separation","source-separation-and-spatial-listening","positional-source-separation","A listener should be able to separate same-instrument parts in a quartet when timbre alone is insufficient and room position carries the distinction.","Same instruments have similar spectra, while reverberation and changing seating alter the spatial cues needed to assign each source.","Train a separator on isolated modern music or rely only on instrument timbre, ignoring position and room response.","Use timbral and positional cues and evaluate generalization to a seating arrangement not used for training.","Represent spectral identity together with spatial or positional evidence, then estimate each instrument while preserving the quartet mixture's structure.","Separation is an inverse mixture problem: the model uses complementary cues to resolve sources whose timbral likelihoods overlap.","A new reverberant string-quartet dataset tests the proposed separator across seating arrangements against state-of-the-art separation methods.","The authors report competitive or improved separation and transfer to a new arrangement, indicating that positional cues complement timbre.","One quartet domain, limited seating and recording conditions, dataset scale, and source-isolation metrics limit claims about music separation broadly."),
"yang25h_interspeech":("voice-generation-and-control","text-to-audio-and-content","retrieval-grounded-generation","A text-to-audio system should retrieve acoustically relevant examples when a prompt describes a rare event, without requiring retraining for every new sound.","Zero-shot prompts may be underspecified and generative models inherit gaps and stereotypes from training data.","Generate directly from text with a fixed model and assume its parametric memory covers rare or compositional events.","Add retrieval-augmented conditioning so generated audio can use examples selected from an external datastore.","Retrieve top-k semantically related audio or captions, inject them into the conditioning context, and compare retrieval strategies without changing the generator's core weights.","Retrieval changes the evidence available at generation time; matched comparisons test whether external examples improve conditional likelihood and perceptual relevance.","Audiobox TTA-RAG evaluates retrieval variants and zero-/few-shot text-to-audio generation on multiple metrics and curated evaluation sets.","The paper reports improved generation metrics while preserving few-shot and zero-shot operation, with retrieval choice affecting the result.","Datastore curation, retrieval leakage, metric validity, prompt coverage, and compute/memory cost limit claims about open-world generation."),
"yang25q_interspeech":("listening-and-separation","source-separation-and-spatial-listening","fault-tolerant-localization","A 3D sound-localization system should continue locating sources when microphones are few, fail, or provide unreliable measurements.","Localization depends on spatial geometry and synchronized channels, so a bad microphone can create confident but incorrect direction evidence.","Use every microphone equally and add hardware redundancy whenever a channel fails.","Learn efficient 3D localization with explicit microphone-fault tolerance and fewer input channels.","Fuse spatial cues with a fault-aware weighting or inference rule, detect unreliable channels, and estimate direction without assuming all sensors are healthy.","The system treats sensor selection as part of localization: reducing the active array saves computation while robustness prevents one channel from dominating the spatial estimate.","Simulated and measured microphone faults are evaluated for 3D localization accuracy, computational efficiency, and performance as the number of input microphones changes.","The paper reports competitive localization with fewer microphones and improved tolerance to unreliable or unknown faults.","Array geometry, fault simulation, room conditions, source count, and calibration assumptions limit deployment claims."),
}
